Z||000000||Seanh||05-05-2001||11:37 AM||||I want to remove my ground F/X panels and modify them to hold neon tube inside them. I was just curious how to take them off since Im at work and can't look at the car. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||05-05-2001||03:53 PM||||*sniff*<P><BR>*sniff*.....<P><BR>Is that rice I smell?<P><BR>(..the opion expressed here is that of the poster and doesn't represent the opinion of this forum or it's owner. One entry per household, offer void where prohibited, your milage my vary)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||05-05-2001||03:58 PM||||I don't see anything ricy about neon's. I think they look sweet sitting at the local indoor car shows and stuff. I'v got an EL scanner under my review mirror, neon lincense plate frame, undercar neon, and Im actully in the process of doing the flexable neon interior. I DO prefer the nice paint job over stickers any day of the week.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||05-05-2001||11:43 PM||||Different opinions I reckon...I think it's pretty ricey..and don't get me started on a neon interior.....<P>Anyway, to remove the ground effects you need to get behind the body panels. The fasteners for the rear effects can be accessed by removing the wheel well lining. The front sections might be accessed similarly. You might be able to access the fasteners for the door sections by removing the interior panels, but I think it's easier to just remove the door skin. You'll have to drill out the rivets along the bottom along the entire length. You can usually rent the necessary rivet gun, or you can buy one through Harbor Freight online for about 18 bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||05-06-2001||07:03 AM||||If you are refering to just the lower ground effects or rocker panel then remove the three cover tabs in the top and remove the 4 rivets. remove the plastic rivets along the lower edge by knocking out the center and prying out. you will also need to remove the 7mm inner fender screws that attach to it in the front and rear wheel wells. There are also two locking tabs front and rear that you can work out with a flat blade screw driver. ||||reg||1
